      "has_ai_overview": true,
      "ai_overview_needs_followup": false,
      "ai_overview_text": "London has a wide choice of major national and independent full-fibre broadband providers offering speeds from basic connections up to several gigabits per second. Major National Providers BT, Sky, EE, Vodafone, and TalkTalk: These household names use the nationwide Openreach network, meaning their standard and full-fibre packages are available to the vast majority of London postcodes. Virgin Media: Uses its own dedicated cable network to provide widely available ultrafast broadband across a large portion of the capital. London-Centric & Alternative Providers (\"Altnets\") Community Fibre: A major local full-fibre provider covering most London boroughs, offering highly rated, symmetrical speeds (up to 3Gbps or more) and affordable pricing. You can compare available plans on the Compare the Market London Broadband Guide. Hyperoptic: Operates across many London residential areas and large developments, known for fast full-fibre speeds and flexible contract lengths. YouFibre & G.Network: Independent full-fibre networks offering very fast gigabit-plus speeds in select London pockets. Mobile 5G Home Broadband Three and EE: Offer 5G home broadband routers as a flexible, no-landline alternative in areas with strong mobile coverage. You can check which specific networks serve your exact street using a comparison tool like MoneySavingExpert's Broadband Comparison or Uswitch London Broadband Deals. If you tell me your postcode or borough, I can check which independent full-fibre networks or specific providers operate at your address.",
